kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "workspace-structure"
purpose: "Workspace structure — project layout, module organization, and directory conventions."
valid_scope[2]: Cargo.toml,src/
requirements[5]{req_id,title,statement}:
  r1,"app-layer","System MUST organize the user-facing surface under a single src/app/ layer: self-contained entry points cli/, rpc.rs, server/, tui/, and gui.rs live at the top of app/, while cross-surface seams (composition, driver) live under src/app/core/. The print mode MUST live under src/app/cli/ as a CLI sub-mode. Built-in modules (tools, hooks, security) compile unconditionally; feature-gated app modes (server, tui, gui) use #[cfg(feature = \"...\")] guards with app-prefixed feature names (server, tui, gui)."
  r2,"feature-flags","System MUST define feature flags with domain prefixes for each optional capability so that non-default features compile out with zero overhead. Built-in capabilities (tools, hooks, security, repeat-detection, print-mode) have no feature flag and are controlled via config.yaml at runtime. ACP mode uses feature flag infra-acp."
  r3,"no-circular-layer-dependency","Agent layer MUST NOT be imported by infra layer; dependency direction MUST be app -> agent -> infra only, with app being the sole composition root allowed to import both agent and infra."
  r4,"unified-bootstrap","App modes (CLI, RPC, Server, TUI) MUST share a single composition function (app::core::composition::build_agent) for Agent construction to eliminate duplicated initialization logic."
  r5,"minimal-default-features","Default feature set MUST only include features required for basic CLI operation (cli, rpc); extended app modes (server, tui, gui) MUST be opt-in or grouped under a full alias."
scenarios[5]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  r1,"app-layer-contains-entries","",the source tree is inspected after the change,"src/app contains cli/, rpc.rs, server/, tui/, gui.rs, and a core/ sublayer (composition, driver); print lives under cli/"
  r2,happy,"","cargo check --all-features is run","all feature-gated modules compile without error"
  r3,"app-composes-agent-and-infra","",a new app composition root wires Agent,"it is the only app module importing both crate::agent and crate::infra"
  r4,"modes-use-build-agent","","CLI, RPC, Server, or TUI needs an Agent","they call app::core::composition::build_agent instead of duplicating wiring"
  r5,"server-feature-gated","","cargo check --no-default-features is run",server and tui code are not compiled and axum/ratatui dependencies are not pulled
